{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces_ast_fixture",
    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces: a minimal consuming model binding NLEV=8 at the import edge, writing du/dt = -D(F, wrt: lev) for a declared interface flux F (shape [lev_nodes]). The plain-D match must fire through the fixpoint (priority 0, where F: [lev_nodes]) and lower to the rule's single-region makearray over [1,8] holding the imported flux-difference aggregate (F[k+1]-F[k])/dz[k]. The model follows the grid's EDGE-ARRAY contract at NLEV=8: it takes the 9-interface (lev_nodes) quadratic-stretch array ze from the grid's shared fixture library mesh/mms_column.esm (NLEV bound to 8 at that edge as well) and derives zc = column_cell_center(ze), dz = column_cell_thickness(ze); the geometry templates are the cartesian_nonuniform_1d ones renamed onto lev by the grid's own import edge, so the expanded document's template registry carries the renamed cartesian templates beside the column wrappers that reference them (esm-spec 9.6.4 reference-preserving form: bodies stay uninlined). The golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST -- including the grid-derived geometry observeds -- across bindings.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "ast",
      "grid:column_nonuniform_1d",
      "rule:face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces"
    ]
  },
